68. StaleElementReferenceException in Angular
This is especially important.

You find:


WebElement element = driver.findElement(locator);

Then Angular updates the table.

The original DOM element is destroyed and recreated.

Your Java object points to the old element.

Then:


element.click();

can produce:

StaleElementReferenceException

Solution
Prefer keeping the By locator and finding the element again:


wait.until(
    ExpectedConditions.elementToBeClickable(locator)
).click();

rather than holding WebElement objects for too long.

69. Angular rerendering means: prefer By
This is one reason I recommend your framework methods accept:


By

rather than:


WebElement

Prefer:


explicitWaitVisibility(driver, locator)

over keeping:


WebElement element

through multiple Angular operations.

